    "slug": "modes-phrygian-neck",
    "title": "Phrygian, and the Dot That Falls Off the Nut",
    "summary": "Flattening the 2 in the window clamped at the nut both gains a dot from above and loses one off the bottom, so flattening a degree does not always add dots — and the G form holds eighteen for all three modes of this family.",
    "tags": ["modes", "fretboard"],
    "readingTimeMin": 3,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-15"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Same frame, one degree lowered. A window doesn't move when a mode changes underneath it — "
        },
        {
          "text": "Mixolydian, and What the Window's Edges Do",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "modes-mixolydian-neck"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " already worked out what flattening does at an edge, and this lesson leans on that rather than re-deriving it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Start at the nut — the A form, frets 0 to 3. Here's "
        },
        {
          "text": "A Natural minor",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", then "
        },
        {
          "text": "A Phrygian",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — drawn as everything in the window, not a grip a hand would hold. Seventeen dots both times."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "live",
      "component": "caged-shape",
      "props": {
        "root": "A",
        "form": "A",
        "scale": "minor",
        "caption": "Seventeen dots, four frets wide — the window clamped at the nut"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "live",
      "component": "caged-shape",
      "props": {
        "root": "A",
        "form": "A",
        "scale": "phrygian",
        "caption": "Still seventeen — one dot arrived from above, one fell off the open string"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What changed, exactly. "
        },
        {
          "text": "A Natural minor",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s "
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " ("
        },
        {
          "text": "B",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ") sits at "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·0",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". "
        },
        {
          "text": "A Phrygian",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "rose"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ("
        },
        {
          "text": "Bb",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "rose"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ") sits at "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " steps down to "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", inside the window. "
        },
        {
          "text": "2·0",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — the open "
        },
        {
          "text": "B",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " string — would flatten to a fret below the nut, and there's no fret −1, so that dot is simply lost. A "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "rose"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " shows up at "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " instead, because its "
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " sat at "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", one fret above the window's top edge, and flattening brought it in from there. One dot gained from above, one lost off the bottom — seventeen either way."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So \"flattening always adds dots\" is false. It adds from above, and it can just as easily subtract at the nut, depending entirely on where a window's edges happen to fall. "
        },
        {
          "text": "Mixolydian, and What the Window's Edges Do",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "modes-mixolydian-neck"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " made the identical point in the opposite direction, for a raise instead of a flatten."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The G form, frets 1 to 5, is the clean version. "
        },
        {
          "text": "A Natural minor",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s "
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " sits at "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "; "
        },
        {
          "text": "A Phrygian",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "rose"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " sits at "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Both step down one fret and stay inside. Eighteen and eighteen. Across all five windows, the G form and the D form are the "
        },
        {
          "text": "two",
          "marks": ["bold"]
        },
        {
          "text": " windows where every "
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " flattens without leaving the picture. Two of them, not one — neither is the only clean window."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "live",
      "component": "caged-shape",
      "props": {
        "root": "A",
        "form": "G",
        "scale": "phrygian",
        "caption": "Eighteen dots, unchanged — every flattened second stays inside the frame here"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That's this chapter's neck payoff, and it's exact. In the G form all three modes of this family — Dorian, Aeolian, Phrygian — hold eighteen dots; in the E form all three hold seventeen. Two of the five windows can't tell the three apart by count at all, and the G form is the one where both of this chapter's dials turn without a single dot crossing an edge. Never count dots to tell two scales apart — "
        },
        {
          "text": "Mixolydian, and What the Window's Edges Do",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "modes-mixolydian-neck"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " said it first, and this is what that looks like from the inside."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What it costs to play: one fret, the other direction. Wherever your hand reached for a "
        },
        {
          "text": "B",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", it reaches one fret lower for a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bb",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "rose"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " — in the G form that's "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·2",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " to "
        },
        {
          "text": "5·1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " to "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". On the open "
        },
        {
          "text": "B",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " string at the nut there's nowhere lower to go, which is exactly why that dot leaves the picture rather than just moving."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
